---
import Page from "../../layouts/Page.astro";
import TopBar from "../../components/TopBar.astro";
---
<Page
  title="Privacy | jsal.io"
  description="What jsal.io collects: your files stay in your browser; Google Analytics only with consent in Europe. Cookies, retention and how to change your choice."
  path="/privacy/"
  ogDescription="Your files never leave your browser. Basic Google Analytics usage stats, only with your consent in Europe."
>
<style is:inline slot="head">
* { box-sizing: border-box; }
body { margin: 0; color: var(--jsal-ink); font: 15px/1.6 var(--jsal-font); -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased; }
.wrap { max-width: calc(var(--jsal-col) + 40px); margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 var(--jsal-gutter) var(--jsal-page-end); }
.policy { margin-top: var(--jsal-page-top); max-width: 40em; }
.code { margin: 0 0 var(--jsal-space-12); font: 500 12px/1.5 "JetBrains Mono", Consolas, monospace; letter-spacing: 0.06em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--jsal-accent); }
h1 { margin: 0; font: 700 46px/1.05 "Lora", Georgia, serif; letter-spacing: -0.02em; }   /* every page title's size, as on the home page */
@media (max-width: 520px) { h1 { font-size: 40px; } }
h1 em { font-weight: 600; color: var(--jsal-accent); }
.policy .lead { margin: var(--jsal-space-32) 0 0; padding-bottom: var(--jsal-space-40); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--jsal-line); font-size: 17px; color: var(--jsal-ink-2); text-wrap: pretty; }   /* the intro ends in a thin line; .policy p below would otherwise zero its space */
.policy .lead + h2 { margin-top: var(--jsal-space-40); }
.policy h2 { margin: var(--jsal-space-40) 0 var(--jsal-space-8); font: 700 24px/1.25 "Lora", Georgia, serif; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }   /* section headings in Lora, like every page's H2s */
.policy p:not(.code), .policy li { color: var(--jsal-ink-2); }   /* the gold date line keeps its colour */
.policy p { margin: 0 0 var(--jsal-flow); }
.policy ul { margin: 0 0 var(--jsal-flow); padding-left: 1.3em; }
.policy li + li { margin-top: var(--jsal-space-4); }
.policy a { color: var(--jsal-accent); text-underline-offset: 2px; }
.policy code { font: 500 13px "JetBrains Mono", Consolas, monospace; }
</style>
<div class="wrap">
  <TopBar />
  <main class="policy">
    <p class="code">Privacy · updated 2 November 2026</p>
    <h1>Your <em>privacy</em></h1>
    <p class="lead">The tools here run in your browser: images, documents, spreadsheets and anything you paste never leave your device. The only thing sent anywhere is basic usage stats through Google Analytics, and in Europe only if you allow it.</p>

    <h2>Google Analytics</h2>
    <p>It tells me which pages and tools get used. It records:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>pages viewed, how you arrived (a search, a link) and roughly how long you stayed</li>
      <li>your device, browser and approximate location (city level, worked out from your IP address; Google Analytics 4 doesn’t log or store the address itself)</li>
      <li>a few actions: finishing the CMS Picker quiz (and its top match), whether you’d pick that match (and which you’d pick instead, if you say), opening a platform page, adding a platform to the comparison, clicking a platform’s help link, and copying or downloading a Redirect Import file (which platform it’s for and how many redirects, never the addresses)</li>
    </ul>
    <p>No ads, no ad profiles: Google signals and advertising links are off, and no names, emails or user IDs are sent.</p>
    <p><b>Cookies.</b> <code>_ga</code> and <code>_ga_Z0BSTC9TT9</code> tell one visit from another. They last up to 2 years.</p>
    <p><b>How long data is kept.</b> Detailed event data for 2 months; data tied to a visitor for up to 14 months, reset when you come back. Totals in reports (like page views per month) are kept longer.</p>
    <p><b>In Europe</b> (EU, EEA, UK and Switzerland, going by your browser’s time zone), Google’s script doesn’t load at all until you choose Allow. Everywhere else it loads. If Google places you in Europe anyway (say, on a VPN), it sets no cookies and only sends cookieless signals until you allow it. You can turn it off below.</p>
    <p>More on how Google handles this data: <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites">How Google uses information from sites that use its services</a>.</p>

    <h2>Changing your choice</h2>
    <p>Your choice is kept in this browser. <button type="button" class="jsal-btn" data-jsal-consent>Change analytics choice</button></p>
    <p>Choosing “No thanks” stops Google Analytics and removes its cookies. The same button is in the footer of the <a href="/">home page</a>.</p>

    <h2>Kept in your browser only</h2>
    <p>A few settings are saved in your browser’s storage and never sent anywhere: light or dark theme, achievements and which tools you’ve opened, which Backpack items you’ve looked at, your analytics choice, the CMS Picker’s Tags or Notes choice, the Image Resizer’s settings and the save folder you picked, and Redirect Import’s platform, whether its file is hidden and the sheet you’re working on, until you press Clear. Clearing this site’s data in your browser removes them.</p>

    <h2>Hosting</h2>
    <p>The site is hosted on Cloudflare, which keeps standard server logs (including IP addresses) for security and to keep the site running. It sets no cookies and adds no analytics of its own. See <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare’s privacy policy</a>.</p>

    <h2>Platform Playbook</h2>
    <p>The team-only Platform Playbook is separate: you sign in with Discord, and only people I approve can see it. When you ask for access it keeps your Discord ID, name and avatar so I can approve you; members’ details and the team’s edits are kept in a Supabase database, for the team’s use only. Ask me to remove yours at any time. It has no analytics.</p>

    <h2>Questions</h2>
    <p><svg class="jsal-mark" viewBox="0 0 32 32" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><rect class="jsal-mark-tile" x=".5" y=".5" width="31" height="31" rx="6.5"/><path class="jsal-mark-j" d="M20 15V20a4.5 4.5 0 0 1-9 0"/><path class="jsal-mark-gem" d="M20 5l3 3-3 3-3-3z"/></svg>Email <a href="mailto:dev@jsal.io">dev@jsal.io</a>. Made by <a href="/">John Salvador</a>.</p>
  </main>
</div>
</Page>
